Mexico has revealed a new presidential decree from Claudia Sheinbaum that will require social media platforms and streaming services to protect children and teenagers from harmful content online.&nbsp;

The decree will give platforms one month to comply, according to government adviser Luisa Maria Alcalde and reported by Reuters. Sheinbaum said the government would support a bill to penalise companies that fail to follow the rules. ... [<a href="https://www.pocketgamer.biz/mexico-orders-digital-platforms-to-shield-minors-from-harmful-content/">MORE</a>]
